{"kind":"FETCH","data":{"headers":{},"body":"{\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"fe403aa2-2a18-4256-b057-b6c53cd4c442\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"What is the central idea of separation of powers in a constitutional government?\",\"hi\":\"संवैधानिक शासन में शक्तियों के पृथक्करण का केंद्रीय विचार क्या है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Legislative, executive and judicial functions are allocated to distinct organs under constitutional limits\",\"hi\":\"विधायी, कार्यकारी और न्यायिक कार्य संवैधानिक सीमाओं के अधीन अलग-अलग अंगों को सौंपे जाते हैं\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"All public power is permanently concentrated in one institution\",\"hi\":\"सभी सार्वजनिक शक्ति स्थायी रूप से एक संस्था में केंद्रित रहती है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Courts alone make, execute and interpret every law\",\"hi\":\"केवल न्यायालय हर कानून बनाते, लागू करते और उसकी व्याख्या करते हैं\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Political parties replace the constitutional organs of the State\",\"hi\":\"राजनीतिक दल राज्य के संवैधानिक अंगों का स्थान ले लेते हैं\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Supreme Court of India, Divisional Manager, Aravali Golf Club v. Chander Hass, Civil Appeal No. 5732 of 2007, judgment dated 6 December 2007, paragraphs 19-24, official PDF pp. 3-5. Direct official document: Supreme Court of India, Divisional Manager, Aravali Golf Club v. Chander Hass (official PDF: https://api.sci.gov.in/jonew/judis/29995.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"fc51fea0-59d8-4d7d-8817-b5f0ddc38482\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which of the following best describes the “machinery of government” in the constitutional sense?\",\"hi\":\"संवैधानिक अर्थ में “शासन-तंत्र” का सबसे उपयुक्त वर्णन कौन-सा है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Only the physical buildings used by government\",\"hi\":\"केवल सरकार द्वारा उपयोग किए जाने वाले भौतिक भवन\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Only the permanent civil services\",\"hi\":\"केवल स्थायी लोक सेवाएँ\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"The institutions, powers and procedures through which the State is governed\",\"hi\":\"वे संस्थाएँ, शक्तियाँ और प्रक्रियाएँ जिनके माध्यम से राज्य का शासन होता है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The election manifesto of the largest party\",\"hi\":\"सबसे बड़े दल का चुनाव घोषणापत्र\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified with: NIOS, Introduction to Law, Lesson 17; NCERT, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 1.\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"faf5a7c2-4d68-4cee-937e-50e97540f8c3\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"A classification under Article 14 is ordinarily reasonable when it is based on:\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 14 के अधीन वर्गीकरण सामान्यतः कब उचित माना जाता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Administrative convenience alone without any objective\",\"hi\":\"बिना उद्देश्य के केवल प्रशासनिक सुविधा\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"A distinction chosen secretly by an official\",\"hi\":\"किसी अधिकारी द्वारा गुप्त रूप से चुना गया भेद\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"An identical rule for every unequal situation\",\"hi\":\"हर असमान स्थिति के लिए बिल्कुल समान नियम\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"An intelligible differentia having a rational nexus with the statutory object\",\"hi\":\"कानून के उद्देश्य से तार्किक संबंध रखने वाला बोधगम्य अंतर\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Supreme Court of India, State of Tamil Nadu v. National South Indian River Interlinking Agriculturist Association, judgment dated 23 November 2021, paragraphs 14-15, official PDF pp. 9-10; Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 14. Direct official documents: Supreme Court of India, State of Tamil Nadu classification judgment (official PDF: https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2017/16734/16734_2017_4_1501_31612_Judgement_23-Nov-2021.pdf); Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f36b36de-f047-47ca-8776-8eb81c85ae32\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"What is the basic-structure consequence of recognising rule of law as a basic feature?\",\"hi\":\"विधि के शासन को मूल विशेषता मानने का मूल-संरचना संबंधी परिणाम क्या है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Every ordinary law is valid even if unconstitutional\",\"hi\":\"हर साधारण कानून असंवैधानिक होने पर भी वैध है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Parliament cannot use Article 368 to destroy the Constitution’s rule-of-law foundation\",\"hi\":\"संसद अनुच्छेद 368 से संविधान के विधि-शासन आधार को नष्ट नहीं कर सकती\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Courts may never examine constitutional amendments\",\"hi\":\"न्यायालय कभी संविधान संशोधन नहीं जाँच सकते\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The executive may suspend all legal limits permanently\",\"hi\":\"कार्यपालिका सभी विधिक सीमाएँ स्थायी रूप से निलंबित कर सकती है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Supreme Court of India, In Re: Directions in the matter of demolition of structures, 2024 INSC 866, judgment dated 13 November 2024, paragraph 22, official PDF pp. 32-33; Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 368. Direct official documents: Supreme Court of India, In Re: Directions in the matter of demolition of structures, 2024 INSC 866 (official PDF: https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2022/12239/12239_2022_2_1501_57147_Judgement_13-Nov-2024.pdf); Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f17fadea-3a26-4ebe-ab25-747e2cf77e20\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Under Article 161, the Governor’s clemency power extends to offences against laws relating to matters within:\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 161 के अधीन राज्यपाल की दया शक्ति उन कानूनों के विरुद्ध अपराधों तक फैली है जो किन विषयों से संबंधित हैं?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Only the Union executive power\",\"hi\":\"केवल संघ की कार्यपालिका शक्ति\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"The Supreme Court’s advisory jurisdiction\",\"hi\":\"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय की परामर्शी अधिकारिता\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"The executive power of the State\",\"hi\":\"राज्य की कार्यपालिका शक्ति\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"The privileges of Parliament alone\",\"hi\":\"केवल संसद के विशेषाधिकार\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 161. Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f0eb8c54-b4f2-4722-97cd-fcbf5c874ba9\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Why does NCERT describe the Indian Constitution as a living document?\",\"hi\":\"NCERT भारतीय संविधान को जीवंत दस्तावेज क्यों बताता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"It cannot be amended\",\"hi\":\"इसमें संशोधन नहीं हो सकता\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"It balances continuity with the capacity for constitutional change\",\"hi\":\"यह निरंतरता और संवैधानिक परिवर्तन की क्षमता में संतुलन रखता है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"It is replaced after every election\",\"hi\":\"इसे प्रत्येक चुनाव के बाद बदल दिया जाता है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"It contains only conventions\",\"hi\":\"इसमें केवल परंपराएँ हैं\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — NCERT Class 11 Political Science, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 9, printed pp. 198-200 (official PDF: https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps209.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"UPSC\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ebf001be-199c-428d-83f8-d264b35ea4d9\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 20(3) protects an accused person from being compelled to:\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 20(3) किसी अभियुक्त व्यक्ति को किसके लिए विवश किए जाने से बचाता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Appear before any lawful court\",\"hi\":\"किसी वैध न्यायालय में उपस्थित होने\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Be a witness against himself or herself\",\"hi\":\"अपने ही विरुद्ध साक्षी बनने\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Provide every form of physical evidence\",\"hi\":\"हर प्रकार का भौतिक साक्ष्य देने\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Face a lawfully framed charge\",\"hi\":\"वैध रूप से बनाए आरोप का सामना करने\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 20(3). Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"e89e4252-8485-4699-bae8-07db63284821\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"When State ratification is required under Article 368(2), it must be completed:\",\"hi\":\"जब अनुच्छेद 368(2) के अधीन राज्य अनुसमर्थन आवश्यक हो, तो उसे कब तक पूरा किया जाना चाहिए?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"After the amendment has already come into force\",\"hi\":\"संशोधन लागू हो जाने के बाद\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Before the Bill is presented to the President for assent\",\"hi\":\"विधेयक राष्ट्रपति की अनुमति के लिए प्रस्तुत किए जाने से पहले\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Before the Bill is introduced in Parliament\",\"hi\":\"विधेयक संसद में प्रस्तुत होने से पहले\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Only after a Supreme Court advisory opinion\",\"hi\":\"केवल सर्वोच्च न्यायालय की सलाहकारी राय के बाद\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026, proviso to Article 368(2), PDF pp. 258-259 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"UPSC\",\"STATE_PCS\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"e2209049-8bdc-4549-85c1-85f5fbdcd528\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"A House has a total membership of 240, and 180 members are present and voting on an Article 368 Bill. What is the minimum number of affirmative votes needed in that House?\",\"hi\":\"किसी सदन की कुल सदस्यता 240 है और अनुच्छेद 368 के विधेयक पर 180 सदस्य उपस्थित होकर मतदान कर रहे हैं। उस सदन में न्यूनतम कितने पक्ष-मत आवश्यक होंगे?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"90\",\"hi\":\"90\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"120\",\"hi\":\"120\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"160\",\"hi\":\"160\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"121\",\"hi\":\"121\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Constitution of India, Legislative Department, as on 1 May 2026, Article 368(1)-(2), PDF pp. 258-259 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"UPSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"SSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"def0083d-22dc-43dd-8213-8fb0ad0cd56a\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which Fundamental Rights are expressly excluded from a Presidential order under Article 359(1)?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 359(1) के राष्ट्रपति आदेश से कौन-से मौलिक अधिकार स्पष्ट रूप से बाहर रखे गए हैं?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Articles 20 and 21\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 20 और 21\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Articles 14 and 15\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 14 और 15\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Articles 16 and 17\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 16 और 17\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Articles 29 and 30\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 29 और 30\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified: Sources — Government of India, Legislative Department, Constitution of India (as on 1 May 2026), Article 359(1), as amended by the Constitution (Forty-fourth Amendment) Act, 1978. Direct official document: Legislative Department, Constitution of India as on 1 May 2026 (official PDF: https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/76b9f1c47176fc65accc160f19c982b7.pdf).\",\"source_metadata\":null,\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0}],\"nextCursor\":\"def0083d-22dc-43dd-8213-8fb0ad0cd56a\",\"hasMore\":true}","status":200,"url":""},"revalidate":300,"tags":["question-batch","question-batch:subtopic:v9:ce181696-b260-40a3-8550-256c074705f9"]}